Chapter: BezierIdentity
  cites Foreword chapter MathLib
  cites Math chapter Bezier

 Identities a Bezier must satisfy whatever the arithmetic underneath,
 so none of these numbers is a recorded output: a curve passes through
 its first and last control point exactly, a curve whose control points
 all coincide answers that point at every t, and a curve whose control
 points are evenly spaced on a line is that line, so its midpoint is
 the average of its ends.

 The degenerate case is the one that caught the defect. Each basis
 weight used to be divided by 1000 separately, truncating once per
 control point, so a cubic at the midpoint answered 98, 200, 298 for a
 curve pinned at 100, 200, 300. The 200 was exact only by luck of the
 products landing whole, which is why one coordinate is not enough.

Section: Points

  pa : BezVec
  pa = BezVec { vx = 100, vy = 200, vz = 300 }

  pb : BezVec
  pb = BezVec { vx = 400, vy = 500, vz = 600 }

  pc : BezVec
  pc = BezVec { vx = 700, vy = 800, vz = 900 }

  pd : BezVec
  pd = BezVec { vx = 1000, vy = 1100, vz = 1200 }

  fmt : BezVec -> Text
  fmt (p) = show (p.vx) & "," & show (p.vy) & "," & show (p.vz)

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("cubic-t0=" & fmt (bezier3-eval pa pb pc pd 0))
    print-line-uni ("cubic-t1000=" & fmt (bezier3-eval pa pb pc pd 1000))
    print-line-uni ("cubic-mid=" & fmt (bezier3-eval pa pb pc pd 500))
    print-line-uni ("quad-t0=" & fmt (bezier2-eval pa pb pc 0))
    print-line-uni ("quad-t1000=" & fmt (bezier2-eval pa pb pc 1000))
    print-line-uni ("quad-mid=" & fmt (bezier2-eval pa pb pc 500))
    print-line-uni ("degen-cubic-250=" & fmt (bezier3-eval pa pa pa pa 250))
    print-line-uni ("degen-cubic-500=" & fmt (bezier3-eval pa pa pa pa 500))
    print-line-uni ("degen-cubic-750=" & fmt (bezier3-eval pa pa pa pa 750))
    print-line-uni ("degen-quad-500=" & fmt (bezier2-eval pa pa pa 500))
    print-line-uni ("math-isqrt=" & show (math-isqrt 0) & " " & show (math-isqrt 144) & " " & show (math-isqrt 1000000))
  end

